SUMMARY: Tesla City Stories: Live Vintage Radio
DESCRIPTION:Doors at 6:30pm | All Ages | Bar w/ ID | Tickets $10-60\n\nTh
 e Tesla City Stories is a monthly night of vintage radio comedy/drama liv
 e onstage. Straight outta 1944. Laughs\, chills\, romance\, danger\, eats
 \, beverages\, live Foley/sound F/X\, 1940's live music\, prizes\, audien
 ce participation.\n\nThe Tesla City Stories return to the stage at the Ol
 d Church Concert Hall Friday April 3rd at 7:30 PM!\n\nFirst up in an all-
 new episode of The Wilde Card Mysteries\, a John Doe\, a pawn shop ticket
 \, and a one word message lead P.I. Jack Wilde to the very height of his 
 career\, but it’s quite a long way down in “The Cold Client and the Conce
 rtina!”\n\nThen we return to the romantic obstacle course that is Blevins
  to Betsy in an episode entitled “What’s In a Name?” Radio stars Blevins 
 DeBell and Betsy Harper are closer than ever to admitting their feelings 
 for each other\, so what’s stopping them? Plenty!\n\nMystery\, comedy\, s
 oap operatics\, and the musical delights of Smut City Jellyroll Society!
