SUMMARY: Fear No Music presents Looking Back: The Feldman In My Life
DESCRIPTION:Doors at 6:30pm | All Ages | Bar w/ ID | Tickets $25 or slidi
 ng scale donation\n\n2026 marks 100 years since the birth of American ava
 nt-garde composer Morton Feldman\, one of the true originals of American 
 music. Feldman’s music asks its listeners to go beyond the conventions of
  musical form\, the familiar vocabulary of tonality\, and the expectation
 s of duration to explore the space between sound and silence\, music and 
 noise\, perhaps even attention and meditation. To observe this milestone\
 , Fear No Music presents Looking Back: The Feldman In My Life\, a very sp
 ecial evening featuring Feldman’s rarely performed epic masterpiece Piano
  and String Quartet. Beginning the performance are two miniatures\, Five 
 Movements for String Quartet by Anton Webern\, and Feldman’s own The Viol
 a in My Life 3.
